{
    "benchmark_id": 201,
    "prompt": "Write a function that creates a client transaction object for a network protocol request. The input should include request_sender, request, transport, and a randomValue integer used to build a deterministic transaction id. Build id as \"z9hG4bK\" + randomValue. Choose a transportType string based on request_sender.ua.configuration: use \"TCP\" if hack_via_tcp is true, else \"WS\" if hack_via_ws is true, otherwise \"UDP\". Create a logger by calling request_sender.ua.getLogger with the id. Return an object with id, request_sender, request, transport, transportType, and logger.\n\n    Only return the code, don't include any other information,\n    such as a preamble or suffix.\n",
    "implementation_details": "Language: JavaScript. Create a SIP transaction object with a unique ID, logger, and transport setup.",
    "fc_tests": [
